<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Hanwha Corp '96 net climbs.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Hanwha Corp '96 net climbs.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)				  455   vs   269</p>
<p>    Net					  12.47 vs    5.95</p>
<p>Dividend in cash (pct, par 5,000 won)</p>
<p>	common shares			   2.0  vs    none</p>
<p>	preferred shares			3.0  vs     1.0</p>
<p>    Dividend in stock (pct)		 none vs     1.0</p>
<p>    Turnover				1,697.81 vs 1,260.83</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			   16.16 vs    11.74</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		  1.64 (loss) vs 1.99 (gain)</p>
<p>NOTE - Hanwha Corp is an explosives producer. Its share capital increased by seven million shares to 31.23 million in 1996 due to absorption of two companies, dividend payment in stock and rights issue. Details about the two absorbed firms were not immediately available.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
